WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.117
Accuracy is not the only result that matters.

00:00:03.117 --> 00:00:09.757
The illustrative comparison shows a small model with lower quality but very low latency,

00:00:09.757 --> 00:00:17.507
a medium model with a substantial quality improvement, and a large model with only a small additional quality gain but

00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:19.913
much higher latency and cost.

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:26.703
That creates the real deployment question: if the medium model already passes the requirement,

00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:29.991
is the extra cost of the large model justified?
